File description:
1) utils/paths.py

Role: Central place to resolve project paths in a way that works both locally and on hosted services.

Key idea: Exposes DATA_DIR (usually ./data) and OUTPUTS_DIR (usually ./outputs). Looks for environment variables PROJECT_ROOT, DATA_DIR, OUTPUTS_DIR so you can override without editing code.

2) data_ingest.py (optional in your GitHub flow)

Role: One-time downloader for the four free, programmatic streams:

OHLCV via yfinance

Google Trends via pytrends (chunked, retry/backoff)

News counts + average tone via GDELT Doc API

Company facts via SEC EDGAR (XBRL JSON)

Outputs per ticker:
data/<TICKER>/prices.parquet, trends.parquet, gdelt_daily.csv, facts.json, and metadata.json.

Why optional: You already saved inputs in the repo; you don’t want to hit these APIs again. Keep this as a utility for future refreshes only.

3) build_fundamentals.py

Role: Turns raw SEC company facts (facts.json) into a daily fundamentals feature table (e.g., revenue/margins resampled to daily and forward-filled).

Outputs per ticker:
data/<TICKER>/fundamentals_daily.parquet.

4) build_dataset.py

Role: Builds the modeling dataset by merging per-ticker sources:

Prices (OHLCV), Trends, News, Fundamentals

Computes features (e.g., returns, rolling stats) and the target (typically target_return_1d).

Splits into train/val/test (time-based).

Outputs per ticker:
data/<TICKER>/dataset.parquet, train.parquet, val.parquet, test.parquet. Often also feature_names.json (depending on script version).

5) trainer.py

Role: Trains the supervised model (XGBoost or GBM fallback), fits an ARIMA baseline, and learns AUTO ensemble weights on validation via a closed-form solution.

Also maps returns → prices for validation/test using the previous day’s close (so plots and RMSE can be in actual price units).

Outputs per ticker:

metrics.json (return-space + price-space RMSE, learned weights)

predictions.parquet (with y_* for returns and p_* for prices)

model_xgb.pkl or model_gbm.pkl

feature_importance.csv (if available)

feature_names.json, feature_medians.json

6) last5_ensemble_plots.py

Role: Convenience “demo” script:

Trains on ~last 1 year (excluding last 5 trading days) and predicts exactly those last 5 days.

Runs two configurations per ticker:

All inputs (OHLCV + Trends + News + Fundamentals)

OHLCV-only

Learns auto weights internally, produces CSV + three plots per ticker:

Actual vs OHLCV prediction

Actual vs All inputs prediction

Actual vs Both predictions (comparison)

Outputs per ticker:
outputs/last5/<TICKER>/actual_vs_pred_ohlcv_only.png,
outputs/last5/<TICKER>/actual_vs_pred_all_inputs.png,
outputs/last5/<TICKER>/compare_all_vs_ohlcv.png,
plus pred_last5_*.csv, metrics_*.json, and a run summary.json.

7) inference.py

Role: Loads a trained model and artifacts (feature_names.json, feature_medians.json) and runs out-of-sample prediction on new data periods (no re-training).

Good for: Quick inference runs once models are trained; can reconstruct price-level predictions from return predictions.

8) backtest.py

Role: Simple walk-forward backtesting:

Rolls through time windows, repeatedly fits/updates and evaluates the ensemble.

Saves metrics curves so you can visualize stability.

Outputs: A JSON summary (e.g., bt_*.json) and a CSV curve you can plot later (e.g., bt_*_curve.csv). In your older Colab runs these landed at project root; in GitHub-ready layout target outputs/backtests/.

9) plot_actual_vs_pred.py

Role: Small plotting helper for Actual vs Predicted curves from saved artifacts (e.g., predictions.parquet).

Use case: If you want custom figures beyond those created by last5_ensemble_plots.py.

10) experiment_last5.py (if present)

Role: Earlier/alternate “last-5” driver. Some repos keep this as historical or for ablation runs. Prefer last5_ensemble_plots.py as the current, cleaned driver.

11) streamlit_app.py

Role: Streamlit UI that displays precomputed artifacts (no training from the app):

Reads outputs/last5/<TICKER>/*.png plots and shows them.

Can also load close-price histories from data/<TICKER>/prices.parquet.

Designed to work with local paths; also includes GitHub raw fallback URLs.

